[resource]
script = ExtResource("1")
title = "Construction"
brief_tooltip = "Build structures at the workbench.
Men gather materials and work autonomously.
Tents, crates, barrels, sleds, and more."
detailed_text = "[b]Building Your Camp[/b]

[i]After abandoning ship, the real expedition established camps on the ice and shore. Tents, storage, and boats were hauled from the wreck and assembled by hand — everything they needed to survive had to be built from salvage.[/i]

Your men will gather materials from the ship, carry them to the workbench, and build structures — all on their own once you place the order.

[b]How to Build[/b]

1. Right-click a [b]Workbench[/b] to open the crafting panel
2. Choose a recipe (greyed out if you lack the materials)
3. A translucent preview appears — position it, then click to confirm
4. Use the scroll wheel to rotate the preview before placing
5. Your men handle the rest: gathering, hauling, and building

[b]What You Can Build[/b]

[b]Crate[/b] — 3 wood, 1 nail. 2 days. Extra storage.
[b]Barrel[/b] — 4 wood, 2 nails. 3 days. Larger food storage.
[b]Tent[/b] — 5 wood, 3 nails, 2 sail scraps. 4 days. Shelter from cold.
[b]Firewood[/b] — 2 wood. 1 day. Fuel for fires.
[b]Sled[/b] — 10 wood, 5 nails. 10 days. Hauling vehicle.

[b]While Under Construction[/b]

• A progress bar shows how close the structure is to completion
• Up to 2 men can work on a site at once — more hands means faster work
• Materials must be delivered to the site before work can begin
• You can cancel a project to get the deposited materials back

[b]Tips[/b]

• Build storage first so you have somewhere to put salvaged supplies
• Get at least two tents up before winter — your men will need shelter
• Place structures within reach of the workbench
• You can cancel and redirect materials if priorities change"
